# Go Binaries and Build Artifacts
# Anchored to repo root so they match the built binaries, not the cmd/atcr
# source directory (a bare `atcr` pattern also ignores cmd/atcr/*).
bin/
dist/
/atcr
/atcr-mcp
/atcr-mcp-ssee
*.exe
*.exe~
*.dll
*.so
*.dylib

# Go workspace (local-only, never committed)
# `go install` ignores go.work entirely, so a committed one would only affect local
# builds and CI checkouts inconsistently. Kept local to preserve in-tree co-development
# of the root module and ./reconcile after the replace directive is dropped (Sprint 33.2).
go.work
go.work.sum

# Test and Coverage Artifacts
*.out
*.cover
*.test
coverage.html
coverage.txt

# Runtime databases
qdrant_fts.db
qdrant_fts.db-shm
qdrant_fts.db-wal

# Local semantic/FTS search indexes built by editor tooling. Tens of MB of binary
# .db files, rebuilt on demand from the tree itself — ignored here (not just in
# .git/info/exclude) so a `git add .` in any clone cannot sweep them into a commit.
.index/

# Environment and Local Settings
# Broad glob so every .env variant (.env, .env.local, .env.production,
# .env.*.local, .envrc, …) is ignored — narrow rules let a stray secrets file
# (e.g. .env.production) slip through into a commit.
.env*
*.local.yaml
*.local.yml

# Operating System Files
.DS_Store
.DS_Store?
._*
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes
ehthumbs.db
Thumbs.db

# IDEs and Editors
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.project
.settings/
.classpath

# Planning Specific Files
# Entire internal planning tree — kept locally, but never committed. Removed from
# the repo and scrubbed from git history (git-filter-repo) ahead of the public
# launch (Sprint 33.2). The blanket rule below subsumes the former granular rules.
.planning/

# Local Claude Code project instructions (kept locally, never committed — same
# rationale as .planning/: this file is the local session's guidance, not part
# of atcr's public git history).
CLAUDE.md
.agents/

# atcr workspace runtime outputs (diff cache + reviewer outputs, never committed).
# Committed here (not just .git/info/exclude) so the rule travels to every clone
# and to CI, where the diff cache (up to cache_max_bytes) and review JSON would
# otherwise be untracked-but-not-ignored and catchable by `git add .`.
.atcr/

# Code review session outputs (verification/ tracked; logs are committed)
.planning/**/code-review/claude/
.planning/**/code-review/multi-agent/
.planning/**/code-review/reconciled/
.kimi-code/

# Python bytecode. This repo is Go, but benchmarks/repo-state-v1/ carries Python
# FIXTURE trees (a case's base/ state), and importing one writes __pycache__/
# beside the source. FORMAT.md requires a case's base/ to hold no file outside
# that case's stated purpose, so a bytecode directory must never be catchable by
# `git add -A`.
__pycache__/
*.pyc
